%description:
TR 38.901 defines no building penetration loss for its indoor-office scenario: clause 7.4.3.1
gives the outdoor-to-indoor loss for UMa, UMi-Street Canyon, RMa and InF, where the base station
is outdoors. A UE with insideBuilding = true under TR 38.901 INDOOR_HOTSPOT got the urban
scenarios' wall of 20 dB or more between it and a base station in the same building, without a
message. The first evaluation of such a link is an error.

Both radios of the NR UE are marked; the LTE one evaluates no link here, so its channel model,
which is TR 36.814's by default and has no penetration loss either, raises nothing.

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = simu5g.test.moduletest.lib.NrSessionTestNetwork

*.ue[*].**.insideBuilding = true
**.radio.scenario = "INDOOR_HOTSPOT"

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%exitcode: 1
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stderr
is inside a building (insideBuilding), and TR 38.901 defines no building penetration loss for the scenario INDOOR_HOTSPOT
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
